  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img height=\"161\" src=\"assets\\st0072_fd9928a57b5e.png\" width=\"210\" /></p><p><img height=\"148\" src=\"assets\\st0072_7a70ddb366ef.png\" width=\"244\" /></p><p><img height=\"131\" src=\"assets\\st0072_e007e168d67f.png\" width=\"230\" /></p><p><img height=\"185\" src=\"assets\\st0072_851a11ec0f26.png\" width=\"238\" /><br /><br />Chloroxylenol is a phenol derivative and hence, can be identified with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> test.<br /><br />The primary amine of sulphapyridine can be identified with carbylamine test.<br /><br />The aliphatic alkyne of Norethindrone can be identified by the Baeyer&#39;s reagent.<br /><br />Penicillin gives test with sodium hydrogen carbonate.</p>"
